WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:11.120
"Pomegranate: A Natural Treatment
for Rheumatoid Arthritis"

00:00:11.120 --> 00:00:13.680
In a landmark case that made
it all the way up to the

00:00:13.680 --> 00:00:16.400
U.S. Court of Appeals before
being denied review

00:00:16.400 --> 00:00:20.160
by the Supreme Court, POM Wonderful
(the pomegranate juice company)

00:00:20.160 --> 00:00:24.240
vs. Federal Trade Commission, a
panel of judges concluded that

00:00:24.240 --> 00:00:27.280
many of POM’s ads made
misleading or false claims

00:00:27.280 --> 00:00:30.720
touting medical studies ostensibly
showing that pomegranate products

00:00:30.720 --> 00:00:33.360
could help treat various ailments,
including heart disease,

00:00:33.360 --> 00:00:35.520
prostate cancer, and erectile dysfunction,

00:00:35.520 --> 00:00:38.080
and the First Amendment does not protect

00:00:38.080 --> 00:00:40.480
deceptive and misleading advertisements.

00:00:40.480 --> 00:00:44.160
Striking a blow to its billionaire
owners, the Court ruled

00:00:44.160 --> 00:00:47.120
that at least one randomized
clinical trial could be required

00:00:47.120 --> 00:00:52.409
to substantiate any claims of
treating or preventing disease.

00:00:52.480 --> 00:00:55.760
If you look at the medical literature
on the benefits of pomegranates

00:00:55.760 --> 00:00:59.680
in general, you’ll see reviews like
this, with diagrams like this

00:00:59.680 --> 00:01:02.400
on the “medicinal effects of pomegranate.”

00:01:02.400 --> 00:01:05.120
But if you dig a little deeper
you see this is based on studies

00:01:05.120 --> 00:01:09.360
like this: “antiobesity effects
of pomegranate leaf extract

00:01:09.360 --> 00:01:11.680
in a mouse model.”

00:01:11.680 --> 00:01:14.400
First of all, who eats pomegranate leaves?

00:01:14.400 --> 00:01:17.039
And second of all, who’s a mouse?

00:01:17.120 --> 00:01:23.031
And if you do have a fat pet mouse,
maybe just feed them less lard.

00:01:23.120 --> 00:01:26.000
Does pomegranate consumption
affect weight in humans?

00:01:26.000 --> 00:01:28.480
If you look at all the
randomized controlled clinical trials

00:01:28.480 --> 00:01:33.040
(meaning human trials), pomegranates
have no significant effect

00:01:33.040 --> 00:01:37.040
on body weight, BMI, belly fat,
or even body fat percentage

00:01:37.040 --> 00:01:41.040
in those randomized to
pomegranate product consumption.

00:01:41.040 --> 00:01:44.880
What about for the prevention and
treatment of cardiovascular diseases?

00:01:44.880 --> 00:01:48.880
Researchers reviewed 25 clinical
trials, looking at cholesterol,

00:01:48.880 --> 00:01:52.240
blood pressure, artery function,
atherosclerotic plaque formation,

00:01:52.240 --> 00:01:56.400
and platelet function, and...
even in the best studies,

00:01:56.400 --> 00:02:00.841
they did not find significant
indications of benefit.

00:02:00.960 --> 00:02:03.680
Here’s a study on pomegranate
juice and erectile dysfunction.

00:02:03.680 --> 00:02:09.114
It was funded by the POM company,
and yet it failed as well.

00:02:09.200 --> 00:02:12.160
No benefit for diabetes
markers and no benefit

00:02:12.160 --> 00:02:15.520
for chronic obstructive pulmonary
diseases like emphysema.

00:02:15.520 --> 00:02:18.560
They were banking on the antioxidant
activity of pomegranate juice

00:02:18.560 --> 00:02:21.600
to help, but that’s antioxidant activity in vitro

00:02:21.600 --> 00:02:24.647
(meaning in a test tube or petri dish).

00:02:24.720 --> 00:02:28.480
To my surprise, a meta-analysis
of data from 11 randomized

00:02:28.480 --> 00:02:32.160
controlled trials did not
support convincing evidence

00:02:32.160 --> 00:02:35.040
of pomegranate intake having a
significant increasing effect

00:02:35.040 --> 00:02:37.760
on total antioxidant
capacity of your bloodstream

00:02:37.760 --> 00:02:39.840
because some of the
most potent antioxidants

00:02:39.840 --> 00:02:42.960
don’t even seem to be
absorbed into the human body.

00:02:42.960 --> 00:02:46.080
No wonder pomegranate supplementation
didn’t seem to affect

00:02:46.080 --> 00:02:47.840
oxidative stress in tissue samples

00:02:47.840 --> 00:02:50.474
taken from prostate cancer patients.

00:02:50.560 --> 00:02:52.400
But, of course, what we care about is whether

00:02:52.400 --> 00:02:55.439
it affects the cancer Itself.

00:02:55.520 --> 00:02:59.120
The strongest evidence for the
anticancer activity of pomegranates

00:02:59.120 --> 00:03:02.092
is said to come from
studies on prostate cancer.

00:03:02.240 --> 00:03:05.200
Unfortunately, early promising
results were not conﬁrmed

00:03:05.200 --> 00:03:06.880
when they were actually put to the test.

00:03:06.880 --> 00:03:10.000
For example, daily pomegranate intake
was found in a randomized

00:03:10.000 --> 00:03:13.280
controlled trial to have
no impact on PSA levels,

00:03:13.280 --> 00:03:14.640
a marker of tumor progression.

00:03:14.640 --> 00:03:18.160
And, indeed, a randomized, double-blind,
placebo-controlled trial

00:03:18.160 --> 00:03:20.320
found essentially no
difference when it came to

00:03:20.320 --> 00:03:23.586
prostate cancer disease progression.

00:03:23.680 --> 00:03:26.480
They were banking on the anti-
inflammatory activity of

00:03:26.480 --> 00:03:28.160
pomegranate juice to help, but again,

00:03:28.160 --> 00:03:30.800
that had been demonstrated in vitro.

00:03:30.800 --> 00:03:34.720
In people, a meta-analysis based
on five randomized controlled trials

00:03:34.720 --> 00:03:39.040
published in 2016 concluded
that pomegranate juice did not

00:03:39.040 --> 00:03:41.920
have a significant effect on
C-reactive protein levels,

00:03:41.920 --> 00:03:44.160
a key marker of inflammation.

00:03:44.160 --> 00:03:46.320
If you look at the forest
plot, though, you’ll see

00:03:46.320 --> 00:03:50.480
all five trials tended towards
lower C-reactive protein levels

00:03:50.480 --> 00:03:54.880
such that the data combined almost
reached statistical significance.

00:03:54.880 --> 00:03:58.160
And indeed, an updated meta-
analysis published in 2020

00:03:58.160 --> 00:04:01.280
based on seven studies
did indeed get tipped over into

00:04:01.280 --> 00:04:03.520
significance and found a significant drop

00:04:03.520 --> 00:04:06.160
in two other inflammatory markers as well.

00:04:06.160 --> 00:04:09.600
Huh, okay. Well, maybe
pomegranate juice could help

00:04:09.600 --> 00:04:12.861
in the control of inﬂammatory
diseases after all.

00:04:12.960 --> 00:04:18.080
But you don’t know...until you put it to the test.

00:04:18.080 --> 00:04:21.920
Osteoarthritis involves the degeneration
of the cushioning cartilage

00:04:21.920 --> 00:04:24.080
within joints, particularly the knees.

00:04:24.080 --> 00:04:27.040
If you take some human
osteoarthritic cartilage samples

00:04:27.040 --> 00:04:29.280
and drip on a pomegranate extract,

00:04:29.280 --> 00:04:32.160
you can show cartilage-protective effects.

00:04:32.160 --> 00:04:35.772
Here’s how much cartilage disintegration
was happening at baseline.

00:04:35.840 --> 00:04:39.920
Add some inflammation and
cartilage breakdown triples,

00:04:39.920 --> 00:04:44.000
but then add more and more
of this pomegranate extract,

00:04:44.000 --> 00:04:47.920
and you can calm things down.
But again, that’s in a petri dish.

00:04:47.920 --> 00:04:50.160
How do we know that when
we eat pomegranates,

00:04:50.160 --> 00:04:52.160
the active components actually
get into our bloodstream

00:04:52.160 --> 00:04:54.534
so they can find their way into our joints?

00:04:54.640 --> 00:04:58.240
Cartilage-protecting components
were found to be bioavailable

00:04:58.240 --> 00:05:02.080
(at least in rabbits), raising the
possibility that pomegranates

00:05:02.080 --> 00:05:05.760
could be a safe and non-toxic
treatment with no side effects,

00:05:05.760 --> 00:05:10.720
as opposed to the drugs currently
in use. But is it effective?

00:05:10.720 --> 00:05:13.440
Clinical trials are in progress,
and so many questions

00:05:13.440 --> 00:05:16.640
will be answered...right now!

00:05:16.640 --> 00:05:18.880
The first and only clinical trial to date

00:05:18.880 --> 00:05:21.200
on pomegranate juice and osteoarthritis.

00:05:21.200 --> 00:05:25.040
It’s not a placebo-controlled trial,
but instead randomized people

00:05:25.040 --> 00:05:28.289
to pomegranate juice or nothing at all.

00:05:28.400 --> 00:05:31.360
Those drinking the juice did report
less stiffness and impairment

00:05:31.360 --> 00:05:34.080
of physical function, but
not significantly better

00:05:34.080 --> 00:05:38.240
than just doing nothing. Shoot.

00:05:38.240 --> 00:05:44.320
But just as I was about to give up
on pomegranates, I saw this study:

00:05:44.320 --> 00:05:47.360
Consumption of a pomegranate
extract suppresses joint damage

00:05:47.360 --> 00:05:52.720
in rheumatoid arthritis. But no...
it was just the POM

00:05:52.720 --> 00:05:55.920
‘Not-So-Wonderful’ company
inducing joint damage in a mouse

00:05:55.920 --> 00:06:00.400
as a model of rheumatoid
arthritis. Come on!

00:06:00.400 --> 00:06:03.200
What about this open-labeled study,
where the patients knew

00:06:03.200 --> 00:06:04.320
what they were getting?

00:06:04.320 --> 00:06:06.640
Eight people with active
rheumatoid arthritis took some

00:06:06.640 --> 00:06:09.360
pomegranate extract every day,
and the six who stuck with it

00:06:09.360 --> 00:06:11.760
reported fewer tender joints.

00:06:11.760 --> 00:06:13.840
But as we learned from
the osteoarthritis study,

00:06:13.840 --> 00:06:16.880
if you don’t have a control group you
have no sense at all of what role,

00:06:16.880 --> 00:06:18.880
if any, the treatment actually plays.

00:06:18.880 --> 00:06:24.480
So finally, we come to this:
a randomized, double-blind,

00:06:24.480 --> 00:06:27.680
placebo-controlled trial. It’s about time!

00:06:27.680 --> 00:06:30.880
Half of the subjects unknowingly
got some pomegranate extracts;

00:06:30.880 --> 00:06:34.880
the other half unknowingly got the
equivalent of a sugar pill and...

00:06:34.880 --> 00:06:37.440
significant improvement in
the number of swollen joints,

00:06:37.440 --> 00:06:40.800
tender joints, pain intensity,
a disease activity score,

00:06:40.800 --> 00:06:43.280
a health assessment questionnaire,
and morning stiffness

00:06:43.280 --> 00:06:46.320
compared to placebo. So, if you
have rheumatoid arthritis,

00:06:46.320 --> 00:06:49.440
I would indeed recommend you
start eating pomegranates.

00:06:49.440 --> 00:06:52.320
Why not just pop pomegranate pills?

00:06:52.320 --> 00:06:54.160
After all, it was a pomegranate extract

00:06:54.160 --> 00:06:56.880
that alleviated disease activity.

00:06:56.880 --> 00:07:00.560
One good reason to stick to the
fruit is that when 19 pomegranate

00:07:00.560 --> 00:07:03.120
supplements were actually tested in a laboratory,

00:07:03.120 --> 00:07:07.920
most didn’t actually appear to have
any pomegranate in them at all!

00:07:07.920 --> 00:07:15.067
Only 6 out of 19 appeared
to be authentic.

